      "traceTextDiagram": "Todo Skill Main Flow\n├── run() entry point \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:251\n│   ├── handleAdd() task creation \u003c-- 1a\n│   │   ├── store.Add() persist task \u003c-- 1b\n│   │   ├── createTaskDependencyEdges() \u003c-- 1c\n│   │   │   ├── graph.Open() store \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:2036\n│   │   │   ├── UpsertNode() create nodes \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:2053\n│   │   │   └── UpsertEdge() create deps \u003c-- 1e\n│   │   └── persistPageRanks() update scores \u003c-- 1d\n│   └── skillout.Emit() return result \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:580\n└── skillmain.Main() skill runner \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:248",
      "traceGuide": "# Motivation\n\nManaging complex software projects requires tracking not just individual tasks, but their **interdependencies** and relative importance. The agentctl task management system solves this by treating tasks as nodes in a dependency graph, automatically computing their importance using PageRank algorithms, and maintaining relationships between parent tasks, subtasks, and dependencies. This enables intelligent task prioritization and prevents developers from working on blocked or low-impact tasks.\n\n# Details\n\nWhen a task is created through the todo skill [1a], the system first persists it to SQLite storage [1b], then automatically creates corresponding nodes and edges in the graph database to represent its relationships [1c]. For each dependency, it creates \"depends_on\" edges pointing from the task to its prerequisites [1e], and for parent-child relationships, it creates \"parent_of\" edges. After any structural change, the system recomputes PageRank scores for all tasks in the workspace [1d] using the tasksgraph analyzer, which treats the dependency network as a directed graph and applies Google's PageRank algorithm to determine task importance. The final result is emitted back through the skill framework, providing the caller with task metadata and updated graph metrics."
    },
    {
