      "traceTextDiagram": "Graph Analysis System\n├── todo skill requests analysis \u003c-- 2a\n│   ├── NewAnalyzer().Analyze() called \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/analysis/tasksgraph/graph.go:42\n│   │   ├── Build directed graph from tasks \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/analysis/tasksgraph/graph.go:73\n│   │   │   └── simple.NewDirectedGraph() \u003c-- 2b\n│   │   ├── Compute PageRank scores \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/analysis/tasksgraph/graph.go:97\n│   │   │   └── network.PageRank() \u003c-- 2c\n│   │   ├── Calculate critical paths \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/analysis/tasksgraph/graph.go:116\n│   │   │   └── computeCriticalPaths() \u003c-- 2d\n│   │   └── Return insights to caller \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/analysis/tasksgraph/graph.go:154\n│   └── persistPageRanks() called \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:1998\n│       └── store.SetPageRanks() \u003c-- 2e\n└── Task store updates database \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/tasks/store.go:659\n    └── SQLite persistence layer \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/tasks/store.go:180",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen managing hundreds of interconnected tasks, how do you determine which ones are most critical? The system needs to **automatically prioritize tasks** based on their dependencies and importance in the overall project structure. Without intelligent analysis, developers would waste time on low-impact tasks while critical path items remain blocked.\n\n## Details\n\nThe graph analysis system transforms flat task lists into a **dependency network** that reveals true task importance. It builds a directed graph where task dependencies become edges [2b], then applies Google's PageRank algorithm [2c] to measure task authority based on how many other tasks depend on it. Simultaneously, it calculates **critical path scores** [2d] to identify tasks that lie on the longest dependency chains - these are bottlenecks that delay project completion.\n\nThe analysis runs automatically whenever tasks are added, updated, or completed [2a], ensuring priority scores stay current. Results are persisted back to the task database [2e] so they can be used for sorting and recommendations throughout the system. This creates a **self-optimizing task management** system where the most important tasks naturally bubble to the top based on their actual impact on the project."
    },
