      "traceTextDiagram": "Graph Skill Operations Flow\n├── run() main entry point \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/graph/main.go:101\n│   ├── Open graph store \u003c-- 3a\n│   └── Switch on operation \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/graph/main.go:124\n│       └── handleAddNode() \u003c-- 3b\n│           ├── Create node struct \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/graph/main.go:153\n│           └── Upsert to database \u003c-- 3c\n├── Query Operations\n│   ├── handleQuery() \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/graph/main.go:129\n│   │   └── Get edges from node \u003c-- 3d\n│   └── handleNeighbors() \u003c-- 3e\n│       └── Get connected nodes \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/graph/store.go:442\n└── Store Implementation\n    ├── SQLite operations \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/graph/store.go:139\n    └── Graph traversal logic \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/graph/store.go:907",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nThe graph operations system provides a **unified dependency graph** that tracks relationships between different entities in the agentctl ecosystem - tasks, sessions, code symbols, files, and memories. This solves the problem of **fragmented context** by creating a single source of truth for how different components interact, enabling powerful features like dependency analysis, impact assessment, and intelligent task prioritization.\n\n## Details\n\nThe graph skill operates through a **simple command interface** that opens a SQLite-backed graph store [3a] and routes to specific handlers based on the operation type. The most common flow is node creation, where the system validates input, creates a node struct with metadata, and persists it to the database [3b][3c]. For querying, the system supports both direct edge retrieval [3d] and neighbor discovery [3e], which traverses the graph to find connected entities. The underlying store implementation handles the **complex SQLite operations** and provides graph traversal algorithms for shortest path finding and cycle detection. All nodes are identified using stable IDs that survive renames and refactoring, ensuring the graph remains consistent as the codebase evolves."
    },
