      "traceTextDiagram": "Task Recommendation System\n├── todo skill main() \u003c-- 4a\n│   └── scorer.Recommend() \u003c-- 4b\n│       ├── analyzer.Analyze() \u003c-- 4c\n│       │   └── compute graph metrics \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/analysis/tasksgraph/graph.go:50\n│       ├── getTaskMailCounts() \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/analysis/overseer/scorer.go:221\n│       │   └── boardStore.CountMessagesByTask() \u003c-- 4e\n│       └── compute weighted scores \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/analysis/overseer/scorer.go:166\n│           ├── normalize critical path \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/analysis/overseer/scorer.go:137\n│           ├── normalize pagerank \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/analysis/overseer/scorer.go:143\n│           ├── normalize mail counts \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/analysis/overseer/scorer.go:157\n│           └── apply formula weights \u003c-- 4d\n└── overseer scoring engine \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/analysis/overseer/scorer.go:51\n    └── combines graph insights + mailbox \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/analysis/overseer/scorer.go:65",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen you have dozens of pending tasks across a project, **how do you decide what to work on next?** The overseer scoring system solves this problem by automatically ranking tasks based on multiple factors: critical path importance (tasks that block others), graph centrality (important hub tasks), unread admin/overseer messages, and recency. This creates an intelligent task queue that adapts to your project's dependency structure and communication patterns.\n\n## Details\n\nThe recommendation system starts in the todo skill [4a] where a `Scorer` is created with access to both task storage and the mailbox system. The core `Recommend()` function [4b] first analyzes the task dependency graph using the tasksgraph analyzer [4c] to compute PageRank and critical path scores. It then retrieves message counts per task from the blackboard mailbox system [4e] to incorporate communication urgency. \n\nThe scoring algorithm normalizes all inputs to 0-1 ranges and applies weighted factors: 30% critical path, 20% PageRank, 25% admin messages, 15% overseer messages, and 10% recency [4d]. This prevents any single factor from dominating and ensures balanced recommendations. The final output is a sorted list of scored tasks with the top recommendation highlighted, giving developers a data-driven starting point for their work sessions."
    },
