      "traceTextDiagram": "Task Storage Persistence Layer\n├── sessionkit.OpenTasks() \u003c-- 5a\n│   └── SQLite database initialization \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/tasks/store.go:182\n├── Task CRUD Operations\n│   ├── ListByWorkspace() \u003c-- 5b\n│   │   └── SQL SELECT with workspace filter \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/tasks/store.go:418\n│   ├── Get() for single task \u003c-- 5c\n│   │   └── SQL SELECT by primary key \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/tasks/store.go:410\n│   ├── Update() task changes \u003c-- 5d\n│   │   └── SQL UPDATE with new values \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/tasks/store.go:386\n│   └── Add() new task creation \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/tasks/store.go:312\n│       └── SQL INSERT execution \u003c-- 5e\n└── Connection management\n    └── Store.Close() cleanup \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/tasks/store.go:190",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nManaging complex software projects requires **persistent task tracking** with dependency relationships. The agentctl task storage system solves this by providing a SQLite-backed database that maintains task state across sessions, supports workspace isolation, and enables sophisticated graph-based analysis for task prioritization and dependency management.\n\n## Details\n\nThe storage layer centers around the `Store` interface which provides **CRUD operations** for tasks with workspace scoping [5a]. Tasks are stored with rich metadata including dependencies, parent-child relationships, session tracking, and review gate status. The system uses standard SQL operations for persistence - SELECT queries for retrieval [5b][5c], UPDATE statements for modifications [5d], and INSERT for new tasks [5e]. \n\nKey architectural decisions include:\n- **Workspace isolation** ensures task separation between projects\n- **SQLite persistence** provides reliable local storage without external dependencies  \n- **Graph integration** automatically creates dependency edges in the parallel graph system\n- **PageRank persistence** stores computed importance scores for task prioritization\n- **Connection management** handles database lifecycle with proper cleanup [5c]\n\nThe storage layer serves as the foundation for higher-level features like graph analysis, overseer scoring, and semantic search, making it the critical persistence backbone of the entire task management system."
